11
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Dennis the Menace (released in the United Kingdom initially as Dennis to avoid confusion with the British comic strip
Dennis the Menace and Gnasher) is a 1993 American comedy film based on the Hank Ketcham comic strip.

12
00:51:16,363 --> 00:51:22,363
It is directed by Nick Castle, written and co-produced by
John Hughes and distributed by Warner Bros.

13
00:55:32,727 --> 00:55:38,727
under its Family Entertainment label.

14
00:59:49,090 --> 00:59:55,090
The plot concerns the misadventures of the mischievous child Dennis Mitchell (Mason Gamble) who menaces his next door neighbor George Wilson (Walter Matthau),
usually hangs out with his friends Joey McDonald (Kellen Hathaway) and Margaret Wade (Amy Sakasitz), and is followed everywhere by his dog Ruff.

15
01:04:05,454 --> 01:04:11,454
Jeannie Russell, who plays Margaret in the 1959–1963
TV series, makes a cameo appearance.

16
01:08:21,818 --> 01:08:27,818
Released in the United States on June 25, 1993, the film was a commercial
success, grossing $117.2 million on a $35 million budget.

17
01:12:38,181 --> 01:12:44,181
Critical reviews were generally negative.

18
01:16:54,545 --> 01:17:00,545
A direct-to-video standalone sequel called Dennis the Menace Strikes
Again was released on July 14, 1998, with a new cast.

19
01:21:10,909 --> 01:21:16,909
A second sequel, A Dennis the Menace Christmas, was
released on November 6, 2007, with a third cast.

20
01:25:27,272 --> 01:25:33,272
The film explores themes of babysitter, based on comic, slingshot.

21
01:29:43,636 --> 01:29:49,636
The tone is lighthearted.
